Analytics is important shortly.

00:23:15.491 --> 00:23:21.590
So, this data exchange stack,

00:23:21.591 --> 00:23:23.030
what it does is,
it's an intermediary

00:23:23.031 --> 00:23:24.425
between the producers of data,

00:23:24.426 --> 00:23:26.110
which is all the sensors,

00:23:26.111 --> 00:23:28.470
and the consumers of data,
all the applications.

00:23:28.471 --> 00:23:30.260
The sensors could be
hardware sensors,

00:23:30.261 --> 00:23:31.680
but it could also be
software sensors.

00:23:31.681 --> 00:23:33.010
Other applications could do

00:23:33.011 --> 00:23:35.020
further refinement of data

00:23:35.021 --> 00:23:38.050
and produce alerts and
messages and so on.

00:23:38.051 --> 00:23:40.750
Really this kind of
an open stack will

00:23:40.751 --> 00:23:43.020
enable very complex
applications in the future.

00:23:43.021 --> 00:23:46.200
Emergency response, we splice
together information from

00:23:46.201 --> 00:23:48.395
multiple diverse sources
and connect with

00:23:48.396 --> 00:23:50.755
multiple different ways of
connecting with citizens,

00:23:50.756 --> 00:23:52.830
crowd monitoring,
accident detection

00:23:52.831 --> 00:23:55.350
as well as prediction,
and preventing accidents.

00:23:55.351 --> 00:23:58.735
So, that is what we really
need going forward.

00:23:58.736 --> 00:24:01.350
To do a lot of these things
you need to integrate

00:24:01.351 --> 00:24:03.685
analytics across video
and other sources.

00:24:03.686 --> 00:24:05.270
If you see currently, video is

00:24:05.271 --> 00:24:07.335
a complete separate
beast by itself.

00:24:07.336 --> 00:24:09.450
Video is separate,
everything else is separate.

00:24:09.451 --> 00:24:11.725
So, we really need to integrate,

00:24:11.726 --> 00:24:14.560
as application developer you
need to be able to consume

00:24:14.561 --> 00:24:15.870
a video stream as a less stream

00:24:15.871 --> 00:24:18.200
coming from other sensors nearby.

00:24:18.201 --> 00:24:22.830
Really this architecture is
something inspired by other,

00:24:22.831 --> 00:24:25.215
this is what they do for other.

00:24:25.216 --> 00:24:27.750
This is a course kernel
you identify

00:24:27.751 --> 00:24:29.050
which enables a whole set

00:24:29.051 --> 00:24:30.960
