01:02:37.591 --> 01:02:38.990
APIs, and so on,

01:02:38.991 --> 01:02:41.200
and the reference implementation

01:02:41.201 --> 01:02:43.230
will be open-source
and made available,

01:02:43.231 --> 01:02:45.465
and it should be
looking at the future,

01:02:45.466 --> 01:02:48.030
enabling future
applications in AI,

01:02:48.031 --> 01:02:51.625
and distributed computing,
and things like that.

01:02:51.626 --> 01:02:53.825
It can't be done by one entity,

01:02:53.826 --> 01:02:55.700
and really needs a consortium.

01:02:55.701 --> 01:02:57.390
A lot of these
problems, probably,

01:02:57.391 --> 01:02:59.335
US have also figured out,

01:02:59.336 --> 01:03:01.940
but I think with companies,

01:03:04.080 --> 01:03:06.730
this is where
the academia comes in it.

01:03:06.731 --> 01:03:08.610
It can be a neutral entity
which can help get

01:03:08.611 --> 01:03:10.520
this kind of activity going.

01:03:10.521 --> 01:03:14.020
This would probably be
something unique in India,

01:03:14.021 --> 01:03:16.030
and this happens
routinely in the West,

01:03:16.031 --> 01:03:17.370
but this will be
something interesting

01:03:17.371 --> 01:03:18.935
if you can do it in India.

01:03:18.936 --> 01:03:22.765
So, with that, I would like to

01:03:22.766 --> 01:03:25.460
thank really good team

01:03:25.461 --> 01:03:27.340
we have in the Robert
Bosch Center at IISC,

01:03:27.341 --> 01:03:30.860
and also these members of
the India Stack Consortium,

01:03:30.861 --> 01:03:32.960
which is evolving, and I hope

01:03:32.961 --> 01:03:35.440
that some of you can also
participate in that.

01:03:35.441 --> 01:03:38.320
So, thank you for the attitude.

